Được cung cấp máy tính cấu hình cao, trang thiết bị làm việc hiện đại;
Cơ hội được đào tạo và thăng tiến tốt trong công việc. Lộ trình phát triển công việc rõ ràng.

Địa điểm làm việc
- Hà Nội: 1A Yết Kiêu, Trần Hưng Đạo, Hoàn Kiếm

Thời gian làm việc
Thứ 2 - Thứ 6 (từ 08:00 đến 18:30)
Giờ check in checkout link hoạt từ 8:00-9:00 đến 17:30-18:30

Cách thức ứng tuyển
Ứng viên nộp hồ sơ trực tuyến bằng cách bấm Ứng tuyển ngay dưới đây.

duties:
Your Tasks
In the business division Electronics, you will be working with the software development team for Autonomous Driving Department.
▪  Analyze system and software requirements; design software architecture; perform detailed software design, development, and testing of product-specific software for radar systems throughout the entire product development lifecycle;
▪  Work with SW-architecture, Hardware-Software interfaces, MCU/SoC/peripheral device datasheets & user manuals to develop, test and debug software in accordance with software requirement specifications and defined development process;
▪  Collaborate with relevant stakeholders to propose and implement solutions to improve the performance of system, including function implementation and system interface optimization;
▪  Perform Software and System Integration activities, work with CI/CD and DevOps systems to verify Software Quality, Utilize AI agents effectively to improve productivity and software quality in daily work;
▪  Complete software module test report and integration test report according to test result;
▪  Primarily responsible of software modules of HELLA ADAS product;
▪  Other job assigned by Department Manager.

requirements:
Your Qualifications
▪ Bachelor degree or above, with major in Computer Science, Computer Engineering, Electrical Engineering or Mechatronics;
▪ 2-5 years experience in Embedded Systems Development;
▪ Experience with Embedded development tools, especially Rhapsody, Helix-QAC, Poly-space, winIdea, DaVinci, DOORS, PTC, GitHub, GitLab and IDEs (e.g. Visual Studio Code)
▪ Experience with simulation and development tools, such as Vector CANoe, vFlash, bash scripting, etc;
▪ Proficiency in C/C++ and CAPL;
▪ Familiarity with 32-bit MCUs, Infineon TriCore MCUs, and the NXP SAF8xxx SoC family is a plus;
▪ AUTOSAR experience is preferred;
▪ Knowledge in Communication & Diagnostic protocols, including CAN, LIN, Ethernet and TCP/IP and UDS.
▪ Ability to effectively apply AI agents (e.g. Copilot, GitLab Duo…), automation, and innovative solutions in daily work to improve Software Quality.
▪ Experience with CI/CD, DevOps practices, and Python programming language is a plus
▪ Strong teamwork and communication skills;
▪ Good English communication skills, both verbal and written.

